# Testing Protocols Rules
# Loaded when testing protocols are required
# Auto-generated by Dynamic Cursor Rules System

## TESTING STANDARDS (MANDATORY)

### Test Coverage Requirements
- Unit tests for ALL functions and methods
- Integration tests for component interactions
- Edge case tests for boundary conditions
- Realistic scenario tests for real-world usage
- Performance tests for critical paths

### Test Quality Standards
- Descriptive test names (test_what_when_expected)
- Comprehensive coverage (happy path + edge cases + errors)
- Fast execution (<1 second per test file ideal)
- Independent tests (no test depends on another)
- Repeatable tests (same results every time)

### Test Structure
- Use pytest for all tests
- Use pytest.raises for error testing
- Mock external dependencies
- Test realistic scenarios
- Group related tests in classes

### Test Validation
- Run tests after EVERY code change
- Fix failures immediately
- Zero tolerance for regressions
- All tests must pass before commit
- Continuous integration validation

### Test Documentation
- Document test purpose and scope
- Explain complex test scenarios
- Document test data and fixtures
- Keep test documentation current
- Include performance expectations

### Test Maintenance
- Update tests when code changes
- Remove obsolete tests
- Refactor tests for clarity
- Optimize slow tests
- Regular test reviews

### Test Environment
- Isolated test environments
- Consistent test data
- Proper test cleanup
- Environment-specific configurations
- Test database management

### Test Reporting
- Clear test results
- Detailed failure information
- Performance metrics
- Coverage reports
- Trend analysis

### Test Automation
- Automated test execution
- Continuous integration
- Automated test generation where possible
- Test result notifications
- Automated test maintenance

### Test Best Practices
- Write tests first (TDD)
- Test behavior, not implementation
- Use meaningful assertions
- Keep tests simple and focused
- Avoid test interdependencies

